#NEXUS

[ lamanna2014a_fig7: Oviraptorosaur time tree, read by eye at full size. Five clade names at node dots are kept as internal labels: OVIRAPTOROSAURIA, CAUDIPTERYGIDAE and CAENAGNATHIDAE (the last two joined by curved arrows), CAENAGNATHOIDEA and OVIRAPTORIDAE; the Bremer values are not encoded. Polytomies: Alberta dentary morph 3-Leptorhynchos-the 'Caenagnathus' sternbergi clade, and the seven-way node from Jiangxisaurus to the Ingenia-Heyuannia pair. 33 tips, 2 polytomies (3, 7 children); 5 printed clade names kept as internal node labels. Sample 6 case (census 2 extended to draw 120, seed 20261231). Topology transcribed from the figure image and checked node by node; topology only. ]

